                <pb facs="0170" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 774/545a.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        O’Brien.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic">January 26,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Bacon informs Mr. O’Brien that Austria-Hungary and Italy have been invited to
                    participate in International Opium Conference, and instructs him to so inform
                    the legations at Peking and Bankok.</p>
            </div>
